Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 10:52:58 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] UDP_conntrack_deletion_timing_issue

[Description]:
 1. Fix for when switching the firewall mode from Whitelist to Blacklist while continuous IPv4/IPv6 UDP UL data transfer is ongoing  UDP traffic was not blocked.
 2. Fix for When deltable is called to delete the only (or last) active Whitelist rule, X_QCOMRule_Count is decremented to 0 in Syscfg. During the subsequent firewall restart, flush_xqcomrule_conntrack_entries() reads the count as 0 and returns immediately without performing any conntrack cleanup.

Signed-off-by: Saravanan B <saravb@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 source/firewall/firewall.c      | 124 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 source/firewall/firewall_ipv6.c |  24 +------
 2 files changed, 104 insertions(+), 44 deletions(-)

